   1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
   2: """ppcrlwimiwidth -- RUNG-3 WITNESS for X(rlwimi) width contamination and high-half insertion defects.
   3: 
   4: DEFECT.  src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c, X(rlwimi):
   5: 
   6:     MODE_uint_t tmp = reg(ic->arg[0]), ra = reg(ic->arg[1]);
   7:     uint32_t iword = ic->arg[2];
   8:     int sh = (iword >> 11) & 31;
   9:     int mb = (iword >> 6) & 31;
  10:     int me = (iword >> 1) & 31;
  11:     int rc = iword & 1;
  12: 
  13:     tmp = sh ? ((tmp << sh) | (tmp >> (32-sh))) : tmp;
  14: 
  15:     for (;;) {
  16:         uint64_t mask;
  17:         mask = (uint64_t)1 << (31-mb);
  18:         ra &= ~mask;
  19:         ra |= (tmp & mask);
  20:         if (mb == me)
  21:             break;
  22:         mb ++;
  23:         if (mb == 32)
  24:             mb = 0;
  25:     }
  26:     reg(ic->arg[1]) = ra;
  27:     if (rc)
  28:         update_cr0(cpu, ra);
  29: 
  30: THE DEFECT HAS TWO PARTS:
  31:   (1) WIDTH CONTAMINATION:
  32:       In 64-bit compilation, MODE_uint_t is uint64_t. When 1 <= SH <= 31,
  33:       `tmp >> (32-sh)` performs a 64-bit right shift, pulling high-half source
  34:       bits down into positions 0..31 of tmp, contaminating the rotated word.
  35:       Siblings rlwinm and rlwnm cast to uint32_t first; rlwimi failed to do so.
  36:   (2) MISSING HIGH-HALF INSERTION:
  37:       ROTL32 rotates the low word duplicated into both halves (positions 0:31
  38:       and 32:63). The architectural mask is MASK(MB+32, ME+32). When MB > ME,
  39:       the mask wraps from bit 63 to bit 0, covering every bit position in 0..31
  40:       (the entire high half). Therefore, when MB > ME, RA's high 32 bits MUST
  41:       be replaced with the rotated low-word data. The unpatched code left the
  42:       high half of RA untouched.
  43: 
  44: THE TWO-PART REPAIR:
  45:   1. Narrow tmp on read:
  46:      uint32_t tmp = (uint32_t)reg(ic->arg[0]);
  47:   2. High-half replacement before the walk loop:
  48:      if (mb > me)
  49:          ra = (ra & 0xffffffffULL) | ((uint64_t)tmp << 32);
  50: 
  51:   *** THE CONDITIONAL MUST PRECEDE THE LOOP. *** The loop walks mb around to me,
  52:   so after it mb == me and the guard would never fire.
  53: 
  54: ARCHITECTURE, PowerPC Book I v2.01:4310-4327 (rlwimi RTL and prose):
  55:   n  <- SH
  56:   r  <- ROTL32((RS)[32:63], n)
  57:   m  <- MASK(MB+32, ME+32)
  58:   RA <- (r & m) | ((RA) & ~m)
  59: 
  60:   MASK(x, y) is defined at Book I:578 as "1s in positions x through y (wrapping if x > y)".
  61:   ROTL32 is defined at Book I:4008 / 4126 as rotating bits 32:63 duplicated into both halves.
  62: 
  63: CLAUSE (e) DISCLOSURE (what this instrument cannot see):
  64:   (1) Model width vs mode width: the probe runs on `-E bareppc -M 64` (PPC970, 64-bit
  65:       model, MSR[SF]=1). It cannot observe a 64-bit CPU operating in 32-bit mode (MSR[SF]=0),
