   1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
   2: """ppcrldimimask -- RUNG-3 DETECTOR for X(rldimi) mask bounds and wrapping defects.
   3: 
   4: DEFECT.  src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c, X(rldimi):
   5: 
   6:     uint32_t iw = ic->arg[0];
   7:     int rs = (iw >> 21) & 31, ra = (iw >> 16) & 31;
   8:     int sh = ((iw >> 11) & 31) | ((iw & 2) << 4);
   9:     int mb = ((iw >> 6) & 31) | (iw & 0x20);
  10:     int rc = ic->arg[0] & 1;
  11:     int m;
  12:     uint64_t tmp, s = cpu->cd.ppc.gpr[rs];
  13:     while (sh-- != 0) { ... }
  14:     m = mb; tmp = 0;
  15:     do {
  16:         tmp |= ((uint64_t)1 << (63-m));
  17:         m ++;
  18:     } while (m != 63 - sh);
  19:     cpu->cd.ppc.gpr[ra] &= ~tmp;
  20:     cpu->cd.ppc.gpr[ra] |= (tmp & s);
  21: 
  22: THE DEFECT HAS TWO DIRECTIONS:
  23:   (1) The rotate loop `while (sh-- != 0)` post-decrements, leaving `sh == -1` on exit
  24:       for every SH (including SH=0).
  25:   (2) The termination test `m != 63 - sh` is therefore evaluated with `sh == -1`,
  26:       becoming `m != 64` always. The mask generated is always MB..63 instead of MB..63-SH.
  27: 
  28:   Consequences on two classes of encodings:
  29:   - Non-wrapping (MB <= 63-SH): the mask fails to stop at 63-SH and runs all the way
  30:     to 63, OVERWRITING the low SH bits of destination RA that must be preserved.
  31:   - Wrapping (MB > 63-SH): the mask stops at bit 63 and OMITS the required insertion
  32:     into positions 0..63-SH, leaving those destination bits unchanged.
  33: 
  34: THE FOUR-EDIT REPAIR:
  35:   1. Save SH in a separate variable: `int m, n = sh;`
  36:   2. Consume the copy in the rotate loop: `while (n-- != 0)`
  37:   3. Circular increment in the mask loop: `m = (m + 1) & 63;`
  38:   4. Compare against successor modulo 64: `while (m != ((64 - sh) & 63));`
  39: 
  40: A partial repair saving SH but using non-wrapping `m++` and `m != 64 - sh` hits
  41: `(uint64_t)1 << -1` at MB=40, SH=40 (undefined behaviour in C).
  42: 
  43: ARCHITECTURE, PowerPC Book I v2.01:4315-4327 (rldimi RTL and prose):
  44:   n  <- sh[5] || sh[0:4]
  45:   r  <- ROTL64((RS), n)
  46:   b  <- mb[5] || mb[0:4]
  47:   m  <- MASK(b, ~n)               where ~n on 6-bit field is 63-SH
  48:   RA <- (r & m) | ((RA) & ~m)
  49: 
  50:   MASK(x, y) is defined at Book I:578 as "1s in positions x through y (wrapping if x > y)".
  51:   PEM:6882 and Book I:4031 confirm "It is not possible to specify an all-zero mask."
  52: 
  53: CLAUSE (e) DISCLOSURE (what this instrument cannot see):
  54:   (1) Model width vs mode width: the probe runs on `-E bareppc -M 64` (PPC970, 64-bit
  55:       model, MSR[SF]=1). It cannot observe a 64-bit CPU operating in 32-bit mode (MSR[SF]=0),
  56:       where `update_cr0` branching on `cpu->cd.ppc.bits == 64` would compare 64 bits instead
  57:       of 32 bits (filed separately as ppccr0modewidth).
  58:   (2) Unimplemented instructions: `rldic` (XO=2), `rldcl` (XO=8), `rldcr` (XO=9) are not
  59:       implemented in the tree's decoder (`goto bad`) and cannot be driven here.
  60:   (3) Full OS boot rigs: no 64-bit PowerPC guest OS boot image exists in the tree; rung 3
  61:       unmodified machine guest execution is the highest achievable rung.
  62: 
  63: SHIPPED CONTRACT: 27 rows; 495 distinct census cells.  The census uses an all-ones source and
  64: does not test the rotate amount independently of the mask bounds -- the pattern rows do.  The CR
  65: row checks readback PRESENCE only; CR0 value semantics are not covered.  No rlwimi rows here.
  66: 
  67: Sentinel: PPC_RLDIMI_PROBE_DONE (plus PPC_RLDIMI_RESULT=n/N, PPC_RLDIMI_CONTROL=OK|FAIL)
  68: """
  69: 
