 222:     #  #493: the wdcaltoffset rung-3 witness.  A DURABLE, RE-RUNNABLE artifact for a
 223:     #  live sev-high defect whose two prior measurements could NOT be re-run -- #481
 224:     #  preserved 201 bytes of OUTPUT with no driver, and a later /tmp run was deleted
 225:     #  by its own script.  Preserved as EVIDENCE: it drives a real guest and is not
 226:     #  wired into a gate, so it is CLASS_RESEARCH rather than a detector owing one.
 227:     #  #494 ships TWO committed detectors.  The second is not a duplicate of the
 228:     #  first: the main probe observes DRQ and the input ring, and a mutant that
 229:     #  guards only the destructive call -- leaving `cur_command` clobbered --
 230:     #  passes all 18 of its rows.  The SIGNATURE probe reads the ATAPI signature
 231:     #  through cyl_lo/cyl_hi on a CD-ROM rig and is the ONLY instrument that sees
 232:     #  it.  Measured: m3 scored 0 red on the main detector and DEFECT PRESENT on
 233:     #  the signature one.
 234:     #  #525 (wdcaltdigin): the SYMMETRIC CELL of #494 above.  That round closed the
 235:     #  WRITE half of one `if` and left the READ half open, so a READ of offset 1 --
 236:     #  the Drive Address register -- returned the ALT-STATUS byte.  Promoted from
 237:     #  regress/artifacts/wdcaltdigin/ and RUN BY gate_sh_rounding.sh, so DETECTOR
 238:     #  rather than evidence -- and unlike the two #494 probes below it is
 239:     #  SINGLE-LEG, asserting fix-side wants against the gate own binary, so it
 240:     #  needs no dated exemption.  Measured: HEAD 14/16, fix 16/16.  The status byte
 241:     #  is NONZERO (0x51 power-on, 0x58 armed) and that is load-bearing: the mutant
 242:     #  that keeps the guard and deletes `odata = 0` returns S, so with S == 0 the
 243:     #  fixed and broken builds would agree and the row would be vacuous.
 244:     #  #525 artifact instruments, arriving with this round.  RESEARCH, not
 245:     #  detectors -- and keyed by their PATH RELATIVE TO regress/, which is how
 246:     #  every artifacts/ entry here is keyed.  A bare basename is not found and
 247:     #  becomes a GHOST: my first attempt used basenames and took the count from
 248:     #  4 problems to 7.
 249:     #  detectors: they are frozen or one-shot and owe no gate.
