 407: 
 408:     # -- #520 alphatbinegsel -----------------------------------------------------------
 409:     #  The SHIPPED detector.  It is CLASS_DETECTOR and it is EXEMPT below rather than
 410:     #  wired, for a reason that is a fact about the battery and not a preference: NO GATE
 411:     #  IN THIS TREE RUNS AN ALPHA MACHINE.  `gate_crossfamily.sh' is the only gate that
 412:     #  mentions alpha at all and is therefore the named home; giving it one is a gate
 413:     #  change owing its own negative controls, which is a harness round, not a rider on a
 414:     #  CPU fix.  Filed to `wiringcliff', the row for exactly that question -- not left as
 415:     #  a silent third state.
 416:     # -- #521 mk48nvramkill ------------------------------------------------------------
 417:     #  CLASS_WITNESS, and correctly ungated: it is RED on the committed build by design
 418:     #  (15/47, all 32 kill rows failing), so a gate row would be permanently red until the
 419:     #  fix ships.  It is also NOT yet the round's detector -- its `msg census' row asserts
 420:     #  the DEFECT'S OWN SIGNATURE and is green only while the defect is present, so the
 421:     #  probe cannot score 47/47 on any build.  A shipped detector must drop or invert that
 422:     #  row first; until then this stays a witness of record.
 423:     "artifacts/mk48nvramkill/opus_mk48_nvram_witness_20260910.py":
 424:         (CLASS_WITNESS, "mk48nvramkill (#521): eight offsets inside the device's own 8192-byte registration reach a default: arm that calls exit(1) -- rung 3 on unmodified -E mvme88k -e mvme187, SIXTEEN cells driven (8 offsets x read/write), committed 15/47 with all 15 controls green, fixed 46/47"),
 425:     # -- #521 mk48nvramkill -------------------------------------------------------------
 426:     #  CLASS_DETECTOR, and EXEMPT below rather than wired.  It is a fast (0.4 s) single-leg
 427:     #  instrument that runs green on the fix today, so unlike a witness it COULD be gated --
 428:     #  what it lacks is a home: gate_m88k_rounding.sh is the only gate on this CPU family and
 429:     #  it drives luna88k, not mvme88k/mvme187.  Giving it an mvme187 leg is a gate change
 430:     #  owing its own negative controls, i.e. a harness round, not a rider on a device fix.
 431:     #  Filed to `wiringcliff'.
 432:     # -- ppcrldiclzero + siblings ------------------------------------------------------
 433:     #  CLASS_WITNESS and correctly ungated: RED on the committed build by design (19/27),
 434:     #  so a gate row would be permanently red until the fix ships.  It is also a FAMILY
 435:     #  instrument rather than a single-defect one -- it already reds on ppcrldimimask and
 436:     #  ppcrlwimiwidth, two further measured defects in the same handler family -- so its
 437:     #  contract needs stating carefully before any part of it is promoted to a detector.
 438:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/opus_ppc_rldicl_witness_20260910.py":
 439:         (CLASS_WITNESS, "ppcrldiclzero: X(rldicl) writes ZERO on every execution -- rung 3 on unmodified -E bareppc / testppc / macppc -e g5, 190 of 190 census cells wrong on the committed build and 0 of 190 under the one-character repair (committed 19/27, fix 24/27).  Also carries a SECOND channel (the record form reports EQ always, so control flow is corrupted too) and rows for the two sibling defects it found"),
 440:     # -- #522 ppcrldiclzero -------------------------------------------------------------
 441:     #  CLASS_DETECTOR, EXEMPT below rather than wired.  It runs green on the fix in 0.2 s and
 442:     #  COULD be gated -- what it needs is a gate that instantiates a 64-bit PowerPC CPU, and
 443:     #  the two PowerPC gates both drive a 32-bit part, selected explicitly in their probes.
 444:     #  (A gate DOES construct 64-bit PowerPC CPUs -- gate 9 enumerates every machine subtype
 445:     #  -- but that is a CONSTRUCTION check with no result oracle.  Recorded because I had the
 446:     #  stronger, false version of this claim in three rows before a seat checked it.)
 447:     "ppc_rldicl_probe.py":
 448:         (CLASS_DETECTOR, "ppcrldiclzero (#522): 24 rows on unmodified -E bareppc.  A 190-cell (SH,MB) census, value rows at SH 0/8/32/63, a record-form CR0 row, a deliberately-vacuous cell showing where the vacuity boundary is, a negative-apparatus control asserting its own liveness oracle CAN go red, and a disassembler cross-check of every placed word.  BASE 24/24, null medium 16/24, EIGHT mutants 16-23/24, ZERO ESCAPES (killtable_20260910/t2/SCORES.txt)"),
 449: 
 450:     #  The frozen copies are the instruments as-run.  t1 is the 19-row form that pass 2
 451:     #  escaped TWICE; t2 is the 24-row closure; t0 is an apparatus failure kept on purpose.
 452:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/killtable_20260910/t1/ppc_rldicl_probe.frozen.py":
 453:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "ppcrldiclzero (#522) table 1: the as-run 19-row instrument -- pass 2 escaped it TWICE at 19/19 (a shift-decode mutant it was blind to BY CONSTRUCTION, and a CR0 mutant that is the sibling handler's own shipping token)"),
 454:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/killtable_20260910/t2/ppc_rldicl_probe.frozen.py":
 455:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "ppcrldiclzero (#522) table 2: the CLOSING 24-row instrument, byte-identical to the shipped regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py"),
 456:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/killtable_20260910/t0_apparatus_failure/ppc_rldicl_probe.frozen.py":
 457:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "ppcrldiclzero (#522) table 0: an APPARATUS FAILURE preserved rather than deleted -- the driver was derived by substitution from #521 and called THAT round's mutator, which replied `unknown mutant'.  The hard-fail refused rather than measuring an unmutated tree, but the table looked HALF-HEALTHY because both mutators define BASE and answered it identically.  No number from it is cited anywhere"),
