1498: 
1499:     #  landiskaux's preserved census: MEASUREMENT INSTRUMENTS, not detectors and not
1500:     #  witnesses.  They produced the twelve-write histogram the row's warrant rests on, and
1501:     #  they are committed because that warrant previously lived in `_scratchpad/` -- the same
1502:     #  volatile path that already destroyed BOTH of gdromexitsix's witnesses.  Preserving an
1503:     #  instrument is not the same as gating it: none of these asserts anything, so gating one
1504:     #  would pin nothing.
1505:     #  #489's mutant applier, preserved beside its kill table.  A TOOL: it asserts nothing
1506:     #  and pins nothing -- it edits one guard predicate into one of three named forms.  It is
1507:     #  committed because the three mutants it applies FAILED to apply in table 4 (their
1508:     #  anchors were built through a bash->heredoc->python chain and one backslash level was
1509:     #  consumed), and this file is the repair: a real file with no shell in between, spelling
1510:     #  its tabs as chr(9).  Preserving it makes the table re-runnable.
1511:     "artifacts/gdromexitsix/killtable4_20260828/mut_common.py": (CLASS_TOOL, "#489 mutant applier: rewrites the case 0x14 guard predicate, no escaping chain"),
1512:     "gdrom_decline_probe.py":      (CLASS_DETECTOR,
1513:                                     "#490: the two de-fatalised sites in handle_command -- "
1514:                                     "case 0x30's data-format guard and the default: arm.  20 "
1515:                                     "rows in gate_sh_rounding.sh's gdromdecline section with "
1516:                                     "its OWN denominator, deliberately not bolted onto the "
1517:                                     "60-row gdrom_default list.  (This entry said 19 and 58; "
1518:                                     "both were wrong -- 19 is the TOCLEN probe's count, copied "
1519:                                     "in, and gdrom_default grew to 60 in this same round.  "
