1596: #  DATED, NAMED DEBT -- not a count and not a silent allowlist.  gate_offline.sh MEASURED that
1597: #  a COUNT pin actively obstructs the shrink it claims to want ("6, shrinking not growing" went
1598: #  RED at 5).  A date expires; shrinking is green by construction.
1599: #
1600: #  2026-09-20 matches the fbpending_bound:2026-09-20 deadline already standing in
1601: #  gate_offline.sh's SM_EXEMPT, so #442's two debts fall due together.  IT IS A PROPOSAL: the
1602: #  owner set the SM dates and set them TIGHTER than the ones proposed, and a deadline nobody
1603: #  chose is a deadline nobody owns.
1604: #
1605: #  These are wiring jobs, not design ones -- each probe already prints a verdict token and
1606: #  exits nonzero on failure.  What each needs is a gate that owns it, its rig preconditions,
1607: #  and ONE clean gate run proving it green before it ships.  That last part is why they are
1608: #  exempted here rather than wired here: gate_hygiene's own comments record FOUR probes that
1609: #  shipped latently RED because the commit that added them never fired the gate.
1610: EXEMPT = {
1611:     #  pit8253_latch_probe.py's exemption is DISCHARGED, 2026-08-30 -- it is now wired into
1612:     #  gate_arm.sh beside footbridge_sites_probe.py, which is the home gate_hygiene.sh's own
1613:     #  bump note named for it ("wants an operator who can run that gate").  The entry is
1614:     #  DELETED rather than dated forward, in the SAME edit that added the wiring, because a
1615:     #  wired probe that keeps an exemption is a STALE EXEMPTION and this checker reds on it.
1616:     #  Seven exemptions remain.
1617:     #  sh4_bsc_width_probe.py's exemption is DISCHARGED, 2026-08-30 -- wired into
1618:     #  gate_sh_rounding.sh, whose `-E landisk` machine it already used.  Deleted in the
1619:     #  SAME edit as the wiring, because a wired probe that keeps an exemption is a
1620:     #  STALE EXEMPTION.  Six exemptions remain.
1621:     "fbpending_drain_probe.py": ("2026-09-20",
1622:                                  "REPORT-ONLY by default: EXPECT_CAP must be set before a "
1623:                                  "gate row can mean anything, so wiring is a design step first"),
1624:     "hpcmips_ctor_probe.py":    ("2026-09-20",
1625:                                  "rung 2, ~8 s, no rig image -- wants a construction gate"),
1626:     #  Both #494 probes are TWO-LEG DIFFERENTIALS: they take a PRE-FIX binary and
1627:     #  a post-fix one and compare.  No gate builds a second leg, so wiring them is
1628:     #  a change to the instrument -- a single-leg mode asserting only the fix-side
1629:     #  wants against the gate's own binary -- not a line in a gate script.
1630:     "wdc_altoffset_probe.py":     ("2026-09-20",
1631:                                    "two-leg differential; wants a single-leg mode "
1632:                                    "before gate 10 can assert anything"),
1633:     "wdc_altoffset_sig_probe.py": ("2026-09-20",
1634:                                    "two-leg differential AND needs a ciR: CD-ROM rig "
1635:                                    "the battery does not build today"),
1636:     "wdc_altoffset_4bit_probe.py": ("2026-09-20",
1637:                                     "two-leg differential; shares the single-leg-mode "
1638:                                     "debt with its two siblings"),
1639:     "wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py":     ("2026-09-20",
1640:                                     "two-leg differential AND needs a poisoned CD "
1641:                                     "image the battery does not build"),
1642:     #  #520's detector.  NOT a two-leg differential and not awaiting a design -- it is a
1643:     #  single-leg 15-row instrument that runs green on the fix today.  What it lacks is a
